Back in the early days, text adventures were among the first computer
games. Nethack came along, and probably provided inspiration for things
like Dungeon Master, Eye of The Beholder etc etc. I always liked the 
Infocom games, because of the humor and imagination, and avoided the
Might and Magic stuff....Infocom are gone now, which is a pity.
 
How about Infocom games get commemorated in Nethack? How about the
Grue as a nasty monster to fight? It shouldn't be a tough change,
just a new monster. Naturally they won't appear except in dark rooms, 
and they have two attacks (fangs twice, since they're fast). 1d12 x 2 
per round? Maybe lighting the room would cause the grue to die, or maybe
it would just flee?
 


